{"result":"{
  "metadata": {
    "id": "318472193",
    "title": "Contentful CMS — Setup & Operations",
    "type": "page",
    "created": "",
    "updated": "",
    "url": "https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/318472193",
    "space": {
      "key": "SFCC",
      "name": "Adobe SFCC"
    },
    "version": 6,
    "attachments": [],
    "content": {
      "value": "Overview\n--------\n\nContentful is the sole CMS across all Zimmermann storefronts (HPC-001). It manages editorial content,\nbanners, size guides, promotional content, and global assets. Integration is via the Contentful Delivery\nAPI (CDA) for all customer-facing pages, with the Contentful Preview API (CPA) available server-side only.\n\n**Architecture:** Single Contentful space with one environment per delivery tier.\nEnvironment IDs match SFCC tier names exactly — no mapping required at runtime.\n\nEnvironment Topology\n--------------------\n\nSix-tier delivery pipeline. Contentful environment IDs map directly to MRT push targets.\n\n| Tier | Name | Contentful Env ID | MRT Push Command | MRT URL |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 & 2 | DEV | `dev` | `npm run push:dev` | zimmermann-dev.sfdc-8tgtt5-ecom1.exp-delivery.com |\n| 3 | TEST | `test` | `npm run push:test` | zimmermann-test.sfdc-8tgtt5-ecom1.exp-delivery.com (to be created) |\n| 4 | OMS INT | `sit` | `npm run push:sit` | zimmermann-sit.sfdc-8tgtt5-ecom1.exp-delivery.com |\n| 5 | STAGE | `staging` | `npm run push:staging` | zimmermann-stg.sfdc-8tgtt5-ecom1.exp-delivery.com |\n| 6 | UAT | `uat` | `npm run push:uat` | zimmermann-uat.sfdc-8tgtt5-ecom1.exp-delivery.com |\n| 7 | PRODUCTION | `master` (via `production` alias) | `npm run push:prod` | zimmermann-production.sfdc-8tgtt5-ecom1.exp-delivery.com |\n\nPromotion order: **dev → test → sit → staging → uat → master**\n\nAlias Strategy & Release Workflow\n---------------------------------\n\nTwo aliases are maintained and always kept in sync:\n\n* `production` — what MRT production tier uses (`CONTENTFUL_ENVIRONMENT_ID=production`). Flipping this is the zero-downtime release mechanism.\n* `master` — Contentful’s built-in alias, kept in sync with `production`.\n\n### Release workflow\n\n1. Create a release environment in the Contentful web UI: clone from the current `production` target, name it `release-YYYY-MM`.\n2. Run migrations: `npm run migrate:contentful -- --target release-YYYY-MM`\n3. Test against the release environment directly (bypasses the alias).\n4. Promote: `npm run promote:alias -- --target release-YYYY-MM` (flips both aliases atomically).\n5. Retain the previous environment for 14 days as a rollback target, then delete.\n\nThe `production` alias requires the Contentful Enterprise plan. The `master` alias is always available as the built-in fallback.\n\nAPI Keys & Tokens\n-----------------\n\n| Variable | Scope | Local .env | GitHub Actions | MRT |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `CONTENTFUL_SPACE_ID` | Space (shared) | ✓ | Variable | ✓ per tier |\n| `CONTENTFUL_ENVIRONMENT_ID` | Per tier | ✓ | Variable per env | ✓ per tier |\n| `CONTENTFUL_DELIVERY_TOKEN` | Per env, read-only | ✓ | Variable per env | ✓ per tier |\n| `CONTENTFUL_PREVIEW_TOKEN` | Per env, server-side only | ✓ | Secret per env | ✓ per tier |\n| `CONTENTFUL_MANAGEMENT_TOKEN` | Per user (personal) | ✓ | Secret (CI service account) | **Never** |\n| `CMS_WEBHOOK_SECRET` | Per env | ✓ | Secret per env | ✓ per tier |\n\n### CI service account CMA token\n\nCreate a dedicated Contentful user (e.g. `contentful-ci@zimmermann.com`), invite as Space Administrator,\nlog in as that user and generate a Personal Access Token under Account Settings → CMA Tokens.\nStore as the `CONTENTFUL_MANAGEMENT_TOKEN` GitHub Actions secret.\n\n### Per-developer setup\n\nEach developer generates their own CMA token: **Contentful → top-right avatar → Account Settings → CMA Tokens → Create personal access token**.\nAdd it to local `.env` as `CONTENTFUL_MANAGEMENT_TOKEN`. Delivery and preview tokens are space-level — run `npm run config:contentful` to populate them automatically.\n\nLocale Configuration\n--------------------\n\nNine locales matching SFCC `config/sites.js` exactly. No runtime mapping required.\n\n| Locale Code | Name | Storefront(s) | Fallback |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `en` | English (AU) | ZimmermannAU | Default |\n| `en-US` | English (US) | ZimmermannUS | en |\n| `en-GB` | English (UK / EU) | ZimmermannUK, ZimmermannEUen | en |\n| `fr` | French | ZimmermannEUfr | en |\n| `it` | Italian | ZimmermannEUit | en |\n| `es` | Spanish | ZimmermannEUes | en |\n| `en-CH` | English (EU International) | ZimmermannEUIntl | en |\n| `en-HK` | English (HK) | ZimmermannHK | en |\n| `en-AE` | English (ME) | ZimmermannME | en |\n\nLocales are created in the `master` environment during bootstrap; cloned environments inherit them automatically. All translatable fields use `localized: true`; structural fields (asset links, product IDs) use `localized: false`.\n\nContent Type Management\n-----------------------\n\n|  | Editorial content types | Studio Experiences definitions |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| **Location** | `scripts/contentful/content-types/*.js` | `overrides/app/components/contentful/experiences/*ContentfulDefinition.ts` |\n| **Deploy** | `npm run sync:contentful` or migration | Imported at runtime — no push step |\n| **Current types** | shoppableImage | CollectionHero, ImageText, ShoppableImage |\n\n### Migration format\n\njswide4000// scripts/contentful/migrations/002-my-change.mjs\nexport const id = '002-my-change';\nexport async function up(client, { environmentId }) {\n// Use the contentful-management plain client\n}\n\nDrift Detection & Promotion Rules\n---------------------------------\n\n* **Contentful roles:** Assign a “Content Editor” role on `sit`, `staging`, `uat`, and `master` that can CRUD entries/assets but cannot edit content types. Only the CI service account can modify content types in those environments.\n* **Migration runner** calls `detectDrift` automatically before applying. Use `--force` to bypass.\n\nbashwide4000npm run detect:drift -- --source dev --target sit\n# Exits non-zero if drift found — usable as a CI gate\n\nScripts Reference\n-----------------\n\n| Script | Purpose | Who runs it |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `npm run setup:contentful` | Bootstrap environments, locales, API keys, and production alias | Tier 1 approver — once per space |\n| `npm run config:contentful` | Populate .env with live API tokens from the space | Tier 1 approver (writes); any dev (read-only view) |\n| `npm run sync:contentful` | Upsert content type definitions (dev environment only) | Any developer |\n| `npm run migrate:contentful -- --target <env>` | Apply pending migrations to a target environment | CI / developer |\n| `npm run detect:drift -- --source <env> --target <env>` | Diff content types between environments | CI / developer |\n| `npm run promote:alias -- --target <env>` | Flip production + master aliases for a zero-downtime release | Tier 1 approver — per release |\n\nHuman Setup Checklist\n---------------------\n\nSteps requiring manual action in the Contentful web UI or MRT portal:\n\n1\n1\ncomplete\nGenerate `CONTENTFUL_MANAGEMENT_TOKEN` for the CI service account: Contentful → Account Settings → CMA Tokens\n\n2\n2\ncomplete\nRun `npm run setup:contentful` to create environments, locales, API keys, and production alias\n\n3\n3\ncomplete\nRun `npm run config:contentful` to populate `.env` with live tokens\n\n4\n4\nincomplete\nSet MRT environment variables per tier (CONTENTFUL\\_SPACE\\_ID, CONTENTFUL\\_ENVIRONMENT\\_ID, CONTENTFUL\\_DELIVERY\\_TOKEN, CONTENTFUL\\_PREVIEW\\_TOKEN, CMS\\_WEBHOOK\\_SECRET) in each MRT target portal\n\n5\n5\nincomplete\nConfigure Contentful → MRT cache-purge webhook per environment: Contentful web UI → Space Settings → Webhooks\n\n6\n6\ncomplete\nCreate MRT TEST environment: zimmermann-test.sfdc-8tgtt5-ecom1.exp-delivery.com\n\n7\n7\ncomplete\nInstall Contentful Studio app in the space (required for Visual Editor / Experiences SDK)\n\n8\n8\nincomplete\nSet up Contentful roles: restrict content type editing in sit/staging/uat/master to CI service account only\n\n9\n9\nincomplete\nAdd CI service account CMA token as `CONTENTFUL_MANAGEMENT_TOKEN` GitHub Actions secret",
      "format": "markdown"
    },
    "emoji": "6835e010-228d-4ec7-b282-f2d9c7da01c6",
    "page_width": "max"
  }
}"}

